# Netlify routing rules.
# Order matters: specific 301s first, then the SPA catch-all.
# Function endpoints (/.netlify/functions/*) are matched before all of these.

# 1) Legacy URL → canonical customer-facing URL (server-side 301).
#    Any old links / external referrers / browser-history entries to
#    /upsell-* and /downsell-* are permanently rewritten to the new
#    branded URLs before the SPA loads.
/upsell-assistant       /rizq-assistant                       301!
/downsell-assistant     /rizq-assistant-special-offer         301!
/upsell-income          /the-halal-method                     301!
/downsell-income        /the-halal-method-special-offer       301!
/upsell-app             /rizq-mastery-app                     301!
/downsell-app           /rizq-mastery-app-special-offer       301!

# 2) SPA rewrite: every remaining path serves index.html so the client-side
#    router can resolve /path, /quiz, /result, /roadmap, /checkout,
#    /rizq-assistant, /rizq-assistant-special-offer, /the-halal-method,
#    /the-halal-method-special-offer, /rizq-mastery-app,
#    /rizq-mastery-app-special-offer, /success without 404s.
#    Status 200 (not 301/302) means Netlify rewrites the response server-side
#    and the browser URL stays as the user requested.
/*                      /index.html                           200
